WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:00.633
First, though,

00:00:00.633 --> 00:00:02.669
CNN's Ryan Young in Nashville

00:00:02.669 --> 00:00:03.636
for us tonight.

00:00:03.636 --> 00:00:04.070
And Ryan,

00:00:04.070 --> 00:00:05.605
you spoke to Representative Jones

00:00:05.605 --> 00:00:07.340
after he was reappointed.

00:00:07.340 --> 00:00:09.642
So what did he tell you?

00:00:10.110 --> 00:00:11.845
John, this was amazing to see.

00:00:11.845 --> 00:00:13.246
We saw it all play out

00:00:13.246 --> 00:00:14.681
right there in front of us.

00:00:14.681 --> 00:00:16.116
Not only from city council

00:00:16.116 --> 00:00:18.184
and then the marched down the street here

00:00:18.184 --> 00:00:19.219
to the state capitol.

00:00:19.219 --> 00:00:20.587
But all these thousands of people

00:00:20.587 --> 00:00:21.321
showed up

00:00:21.321 --> 00:00:22.689
to be here for a rally

00:00:22.689 --> 00:00:23.790
to walk up the stairs

00:00:23.790 --> 00:00:24.824
here to the state capitol.

00:00:24.824 --> 00:00:26.726
And this all played out right for us

00:00:26.726 --> 00:00:27.961
right there at the state capitol.

00:00:27.961 --> 00:00:28.762
That's where he was

00:00:28.762 --> 00:00:30.897
sworn in on those steps.

00:00:30.897 --> 00:00:32.665
People were cheering. They were yelling.

00:00:32.665 --> 00:00:33.900
They said they wanted their voices

00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:34.801
to be heard.

00:00:34.801 --> 00:00:35.335
And let's just say

00:00:35.335 --> 00:00:36.870
this, just as Owens says,

00:00:36.870 --> 00:00:39.139
he was energized by what happened.

00:00:39.339 --> 00:00:39.739
And he said

00:00:39.739 --> 00:00:41.341
the fight is not over just yet.

00:00:41.341 --> 00:00:43.643
Take a listen.

00:00:44.744 --> 00:00:45.678
Today, we send a clear

00:00:45.678 --> 00:00:47.781
message to Speaker Cameron Sexton

00:00:47.781 --> 00:00:49.582
that the people will not allow his

00:00:49.582 --> 00:00:51.618
his crimes against democracy to happen

00:00:51.918 --> 00:00:52.986
without challenge.

00:00:52.986 --> 00:00:54.721
We are calling on House Speaker Cameron

00:00:54.721 --> 00:01:00.226
Sexton to resign as speaker of the House.

00:01:01.828 --> 00:01:05.532
He is an enemy of democracy.

00:01:06.166 --> 00:01:06.866
And, John,

00:01:06.866 --> 00:01:08.101
more than a thousand people

00:01:08.101 --> 00:01:09.302
marched with him

00:01:09.302 --> 00:01:10.703
all the way from city hall

00:01:10.703 --> 00:01:12.372
and then walk through that front door.

00:01:12.372 --> 00:01:14.541
And then, of course, when they swore him

00:01:14.541 --> 00:01:16.109
right there on the steps that he went

00:01:16.109 --> 00:01:17.577
and got his old plaque back

00:01:17.577 --> 00:01:18.745
and went into that seat.

00:01:18.745 --> 00:01:19.479
The battle here

00:01:19.479 --> 00:01:20.747
won't stop for quite some time

00:01:20.747 --> 00:01:21.948
because that remember,

00:01:21.948 --> 00:01:23.817
they were appointed back to the seat

00:01:23.817 --> 00:01:24.484
and we're told

00:01:24.484 --> 00:01:26.653
there will have to be a special election.

00:01:26.653 --> 00:01:28.888
So this process is not over just yet.

00:01:29.089 --> 00:01:30.723
But you can just tell by the energy

00:01:30.723 --> 00:01:32.325
that's surrounding the city right now

00:01:32.325 --> 00:01:33.359
that they believe

00:01:33.359 --> 00:01:34.794
they have finally sort of cracked

00:01:34.794 --> 00:01:35.662
the surface in terms

00:01:35.662 --> 00:01:36.963
of getting people to understand

00:01:36.963 --> 00:01:38.331
what's going on in the state

00:01:38.331 --> 00:01:39.666
in this process tonight

00:01:39.666 --> 00:01:40.433
that you just saw

00:01:40.433 --> 00:01:42.469
was for Representative Jones.

00:01:42.836 --> 00:01:43.303
In a moment,

00:01:43.303 --> 00:01:43.770
I'm going to speak

00:01:43.770 --> 00:01:45.238
to Representative Justin Pierson.

00:01:45.238 --> 00:01:46.206
What's the timetable

00:01:46.206 --> 00:01:49.342
for his possible reinstatement?

00:01:49.476 --> 00:01:51.244
Well, they are talking about Wednesday.

00:01:51.244 --> 00:01:52.112
So, of course,

00:01:52.112 --> 00:01:53.012
there was this talk

00:01:53.012 --> 00:01:53.713
across the state

00:01:53.713 --> 00:01:55.048
about whether or not

00:01:55.048 --> 00:01:55.949
what could happen here

00:01:55.949 --> 00:01:56.649
at the state house

00:01:56.649 --> 00:01:57.750
might affect

00:01:57.750 --> 00:01:58.384
Shelby County

00:01:58.384 --> 00:01:59.752
and whether or not funds

00:01:59.752 --> 00:02:00.720
would be held back.

00:02:00.720 --> 00:02:01.754
But now we're hearing,

00:02:01.754 --> 00:02:03.123
we believe that

00:02:03.123 --> 00:02:04.324
what will happen in Memphis,

00:02:04.324 --> 00:02:06.392
Will Pierson will be get a chance

00:02:06.526 --> 00:02:07.560
to come back to the house.

00:02:07.560 --> 00:02:08.661
But he was here today

00:02:08.661 --> 00:02:10.430
to energize the crowd

00:02:10.430 --> 00:02:11.998
and see both these young men

00:02:11.998 --> 00:02:13.533
standing together strong,

00:02:13.533 --> 00:02:14.901
addressing this crowd.

00:02:14.901 --> 00:02:16.503
The crowd came to hear these two people.

00:02:16.503 --> 00:02:17.337
At some point,

00:02:17.337 --> 00:02:19.405
it sounded like they were addressing

00:02:19.405 --> 00:02:20.440
like a rock concert

00:02:20.440 --> 00:02:21.608
because it was so loud

00:02:21.608 --> 00:02:22.242
here with

00:02:22.242 --> 00:02:23.409
people amped up

00:02:23.409 --> 00:02:25.378
and pumped up to go into the statehouse.

00:02:25.378 --> 00:02:26.546
People admitted to us today

00:02:26.546 --> 00:02:28.381
they had never been to the state capitol,

00:02:28.381 --> 00:02:29.282
but they wanted to be here

00:02:29.282 --> 00:02:30.683
to support these two young men

00:02:30.683 --> 00:02:32.752
who they felt like were unjustifiably

00:02:32.752 --> 00:02:34.420
kicked out of the statehouse last week.

00:02:34.420 --> 00:02:36.189
Two elected officials

00:02:36.189 --> 00:02:38.658
both expelled, one now reinstate dated.

00:02:38.791 --> 00:02:40.894
Ryan Young, thank you very much.

00:02:40.894 --> 00:02:41.961
Now to the other.

00:02:41.961 --> 00:02:42.662
Joining us now,

00:02:42.662 --> 00:02:44.197
the man in question, Representative

00:02:44.197 --> 00:02:45.298
Justin Jay Pierson.

00:02:45.298 --> 00:02:45.832
Representative,

00:02:45.832 --> 00:02:47.233
thanks so much for being with us.

00:02:47.233 --> 00:02:47.901
Your reaction

00:02:47.901 --> 00:02:48.902
tonight to your colleague

00:02:48.902 --> 00:02:50.103
being reappointed

00:02:50.103 --> 00:02:51.271
to the Tennessee legislature

00:02:51.271 --> 00:02:52.305
and are you confident

00:02:52.305 --> 00:02:55.642
that you will be reinstated on Wednesday?

00:02:56.809 --> 00:02:58.378
First, I want to

00:02:58.378 --> 00:02:58.912
honor the

00:02:58.912 --> 00:03:00.079
victims of another mass

00:03:00.079 --> 00:03:02.282
shooting in our country in Louisville

00:03:02.282 --> 00:03:05.218
and the mass shooting here in Nashville

00:03:05.218 --> 00:03:06.052
at the Covenant School

00:03:06.052 --> 00:03:08.454
that elevated this real conversation

00:03:08.454 --> 00:03:09.656
for the need to end gun violence

00:03:09.656 --> 00:03:10.390
in our communities.

00:03:10.390 --> 00:03:11.958
That's the issue that we got expelled

00:03:11.958 --> 00:03:12.692
for standing up

00:03:12.692 --> 00:03:14.561
against the National Rifle Association

00:03:14.561 --> 00:03:16.162
and standing up against gun lobbyists

00:03:16.162 --> 00:03:17.163
and so on.

00:03:17.163 --> 00:03:18.631
I still mourn

00:03:18.631 --> 00:03:20.200
with everyone who is still mourning.

00:03:20.200 --> 00:03:21.768
And while we celebrate

00:03:21.768 --> 00:03:23.469
our brother, Representative Jones,

00:03:23.469 --> 00:03:25.738
and the democratic process of people

00:03:25.738 --> 00:03:26.673
who have decided

00:03:26.673 --> 00:03:27.173
that we are

00:03:27.173 --> 00:03:28.374
tired of the injustice

00:03:28.374 --> 00:03:29.676
of the Republican majority

00:03:29.676 --> 00:03:31.311
of the Tennessee Statehouse

00:03:31.311 --> 00:03:32.011
who are deciding

00:03:32.011 --> 00:03:33.713
that they are going to have a mob ocracy

00:03:33.713 --> 00:03:35.648
rather than a democracy.

00:03:35.648 --> 00:03:37.850
We continue this fight and this movement

00:03:37.850 --> 00:03:39.285
and this momentum toward justice.

00:03:40.587 --> 00:03:43.323
How do you think you will be received

00:03:43.690 --> 00:03:44.991
given that you were voted out

00:03:44.991 --> 00:03:46.759
by a super majority if you are

00:03:46.759 --> 00:03:48.795
and you are reinstated on Wednesday?

00:03:48.795 --> 00:03:50.330
How do you think that Republican

00:03:50.330 --> 00:03:53.233
majority will greet you?

00:03:54.267 --> 00:03:55.401
I don't know exactly

00:03:55.401 --> 00:03:56.402
how the Republican Party

00:03:56.402 --> 00:03:57.870
is going to greet us into the future.

00:03:57.870 --> 00:03:59.172
What I do know is that the people

00:03:59.172 --> 00:04:00.840
who are advocating for change,

00:04:00.840 --> 00:04:01.241
the people

00:04:01.241 --> 00:04:02.909
who want to see an end to gun violence,

00:04:02.909 --> 00:04:04.310
the people who are asking

00:04:04.310 --> 00:04:05.211
that our legislators

00:04:05.211 --> 00:04:05.878
do something,

00:04:05.878 --> 00:04:07.480
the people who continue to march

00:04:07.480 --> 00:04:08.248
and to protest

00:04:08.248 --> 00:04:08.781
and who continue

00:04:08.781 --> 00:04:10.016
to show up, the children

00:04:10.016 --> 00:04:11.484
and the teenagers and the grandmothers

00:04:11.484 --> 00:04:12.752
who the Republican Party called

00:04:12.752 --> 00:04:14.153
insurrectionists who were peaceful

00:04:14.153 --> 00:04:15.622
protesters are going to continue

00:04:15.622 --> 00:04:17.357
to demand that justice happen.

00:04:17.357 --> 00:04:18.391
And if I have the opportunity

00:04:18.391 --> 00:04:19.559
to serve the people of Memphis

00:04:19.559 --> 00:04:21.094
and Millington in Shelby County

00:04:21.094 --> 00:04:22.161
as District 86

00:04:22.161 --> 00:04:23.763
is representative in this appointment

00:04:23.763 --> 00:04:25.198
and hopefully in an elected office,

00:04:25.198 --> 00:04:26.332
I promise to elevate

00:04:26.332 --> 00:04:28.234
the issues of our community and not stop

00:04:28.234 --> 00:04:29.636
because the issues of justice

00:04:29.636 --> 00:04:30.837
in the state of Tennessee

00:04:30.837 --> 00:04:32.739
and a state that too often is silencing

00:04:32.739 --> 00:04:34.040
those who are marginalized,

00:04:34.040 --> 00:04:35.608
that is intentionally expelling

00:04:35.608 --> 00:04:36.576
voices of people

00:04:36.576 --> 00:04:37.043
who are saying

00:04:37.043 --> 00:04:38.378
we have to do something about gun

00:04:38.378 --> 00:04:39.646
violence, who are exercising

00:04:39.646 --> 00:04:40.513
our First Amendment

00:04:40.513 --> 00:04:42.448
that is given to us in the Constitution.

00:04:42.448 --> 00:04:44.617
If it is the will of God

00:04:44.617 --> 00:04:46.085
and the people in Shelby County

00:04:46.085 --> 00:04:46.786
for me to serve,

00:04:46.786 --> 00:04:48.354
I promise to continue to do so.

00:04:48.354 --> 00:04:49.188
And I'm going to do it,

00:04:49.188 --> 00:04:49.756
I believe,

00:04:49.756 --> 00:04:51.157
with all of the people who continue

00:04:51.157 --> 00:04:52.625
to show up for us in this moment

00:04:52.625 --> 00:04:53.793
who are saying it's enough

00:04:53.793 --> 00:04:54.961
and now is the time

00:04:54.961 --> 00:04:56.996
for us to create change in this state.

00:04:56.996 --> 00:04:57.697
Talk to me about

00:04:57.697 --> 00:04:59.032
maybe the split feelings

00:04:59.032 --> 00:05:00.400
that you brought up yourself

00:05:00.400 --> 00:05:02.068
to see your colleague reinstate

00:05:02.068 --> 00:05:03.469
voted today,

00:05:03.469 --> 00:05:07.140
but also today to see a mass shooting

00:05:07.140 --> 00:05:09.208
where four people were gunned down

00:05:09.509 --> 00:05:11.744
in a neighboring state.

00:05:13.413 --> 00:05:15.948
It's a sobering reality that we are in

00:05:16.282 --> 00:05:18.084
that we are not doing enough

00:05:18.084 --> 00:05:19.852
to prevent gun violence.

00:05:19.852 --> 00:05:21.087
It is a sad

00:05:21.087 --> 00:05:22.789
and another tragic day in our country

00:05:22.789 --> 00:05:24.257
where we know the decisions of people

00:05:24.257 --> 00:05:25.425
in power,

00:05:25.425 --> 00:05:26.693
decisions of people

00:05:26.693 --> 00:05:28.061
who could actually do something

00:05:28.061 --> 00:05:29.462
to prevent gun violence

00:05:29.462 --> 00:05:30.563
in our schools,

00:05:30.563 --> 00:05:32.265
in our banks, in our communities

00:05:32.265 --> 00:05:33.166
by preventing guns

00:05:33.166 --> 00:05:34.567
from getting in the hands of individuals

00:05:34.567 --> 00:05:35.234
who have them.

00:05:35.234 --> 00:05:36.602
The people in positions of power

00:05:36.602 --> 00:05:38.171
are refusing to act.

00:05:38.171 --> 00:05:39.238
And it is a tragedy

00:05:39.238 --> 00:05:40.740
that that is our reality.

00:05:40.740 --> 00:05:41.507
And at the same time,

00:05:41.507 --> 00:05:42.642
we are seeing people

00:05:42.642 --> 00:05:44.010
who are pleading for democracy

00:05:44.010 --> 00:05:45.011
to work, the people

00:05:45.011 --> 00:05:46.346
and Nashville Metro Council,

00:05:46.346 --> 00:05:47.747
the people in Shelby County

00:05:47.747 --> 00:05:48.815
that the county commission.

00:05:48.815 --> 00:05:49.549
Our communities

00:05:49.549 --> 00:05:50.583
are pleading for democracy

00:05:50.583 --> 00:05:51.918
to work in order that we might be able

00:05:51.918 --> 00:05:53.686
to effect the change that we need.

00:05:53.686 --> 00:05:54.287
And so, yes,

00:05:54.287 --> 00:05:57.023
it is multiple emotions, a celebration,

00:05:57.023 --> 00:05:58.358
and of the determination

00:05:58.358 --> 00:06:00.093
of a people who want to see justice

00:06:00.093 --> 00:06:01.427
happen with representative Jones

00:06:01.427 --> 00:06:02.328
being receded.

00:06:02.328 --> 00:06:03.730
And it also a painful moment

00:06:03.730 --> 00:06:04.397
of recognition

00:06:04.397 --> 00:06:06.132
that our legislators and people

00:06:06.132 --> 00:06:07.066
like Cameron Sexton

00:06:07.066 --> 00:06:08.167
and the Republican Party

00:06:08.167 --> 00:06:08.701
in Tennessee

00:06:08.701 --> 00:06:10.303
and across the South in this country

00:06:10.303 --> 00:06:11.938
are not doing nearly enough

00:06:11.938 --> 00:06:12.672
to prevent guns

00:06:12.672 --> 00:06:13.806
from getting in the hands of people

00:06:13.806 --> 00:06:15.441
and doing all of the holistic work

00:06:15.441 --> 00:06:16.242
of gun prevention

00:06:16.242 --> 00:06:17.210
that is necessary

00:06:17.210 --> 00:06:18.745
in places across our communities,

00:06:18.745 --> 00:06:20.680
including in Memphis and Millington.

00:06:20.680 --> 00:06:21.381
My district,

00:06:21.381 --> 00:06:23.483
very quickly, if you are reinstated,

00:06:24.150 --> 00:06:27.086
would you engage in the type of behavior

00:06:27.086 --> 00:06:28.388
that Republicans say

00:06:28.388 --> 00:06:29.789
they expelled you for?

00:06:29.789 --> 00:06:32.925
Would you demonstrate again like you did

00:06:33.393 --> 00:06:36.129
on the House floor?

00:06:36.262 --> 00:06:37.430
I believe that our actions

00:06:37.430 --> 00:06:38.798
were wholly justified

00:06:38.798 --> 00:06:39.766
and that even though

00:06:39.766 --> 00:06:40.933
we broke a rule of decorum,

00:06:40.933 --> 00:06:42.635
we stood up and we spoke for people

00:06:42.635 --> 00:06:43.970
who needed us to speak for them.

00:06:43.970 --> 00:06:45.838
Voices of children and adults

00:06:45.838 --> 00:06:47.507
who will never be able to speak again.

00:06:47.507 --> 00:06:49.242
And so I believe what we did was right

00:06:49.242 --> 00:06:50.376
and it was for right.

00:06:50.376 --> 00:06:52.111
And that we have a responsibility now.

00:06:52.111 --> 00:06:52.979
And our legislators

00:06:52.979 --> 00:06:53.379
in this

00:06:53.379 --> 00:06:54.680
legislature, legislator

00:06:54.680 --> 00:06:57.450
now need to do more to stop it in

00:06:57.450 --> 00:06:58.084
gun violence.

00:06:58.084 --> 00:06:59.185
It is preventable

00:06:59.185 --> 00:07:00.887
and we aren't doing nearly enough.

00:07:00.887 --> 00:07:01.254
Would you

00:07:01.254 --> 00:07:02.588
break the rules of decorum again

00:07:02.588 --> 00:07:05.158
to make that point?

00:07:05.224 --> 00:07:06.959
Sometimes rules have to be broken

00:07:06.959 --> 00:07:07.260
in order

00:07:07.260 --> 00:07:07.760
for the people

00:07:07.760 --> 00:07:09.128
who've been pushed to the periphery

00:07:09.128 --> 00:07:09.629
to be brought

00:07:09.629 --> 00:07:11.297
to the center of the conversation.

00:07:11.297 --> 00:07:13.032
Sometimes rules have to be broken

00:07:13.032 --> 00:07:13.433
in order

00:07:13.433 --> 00:07:14.066
for the voices

00:07:14.066 --> 00:07:15.835
that have been marginalized, told

00:07:15.835 --> 00:07:17.370
that they are voiceless to be heard.

00:07:17.370 --> 00:07:18.871
Sometimes rules have to be broken

00:07:18.871 --> 00:07:20.440
in order for us to create justice.

00:07:20.440 --> 00:07:21.674
And if that is what's necessary

00:07:21.674 --> 00:07:22.942
for justice to happen, then

00:07:22.942 --> 00:07:24.243
that is what is necessary.

00:07:24.243 --> 00:07:25.011
And as you see

00:07:25.011 --> 00:07:26.512
District 86 in our community,

00:07:26.512 --> 00:07:28.080
we're willing to risk it all

00:07:28.080 --> 00:07:28.981
for people to be safe.

00:07:28.981 --> 00:07:30.616
We're willing to risk it all for justice

00:07:30.616 --> 00:07:31.651
to roll down like waters

00:07:31.651 --> 00:07:32.251
and righteousness

00:07:32.251 --> 00:07:33.419
like a never flowing stream.

00:07:33.419 --> 00:07:35.221
And we will not stop

00:07:35.221 --> 00:07:37.790
events like we have not seen happening

00:07:37.790 --> 00:07:39.425
in Nashville before our eyes.

00:07:39.425 --> 00:07:40.293
Representative Pierson,

00:07:40.293 --> 00:07:41.461
we do appreciate you

00:07:41.461 --> 00:07:42.628
being with us tonight.

00:07:42.628 --> 00:07:44.397
Look forward to speaking with you again.

00:07:46.299 --> 00:07:46.666
Thank you.

00:07:46.666 --> 00:07:47.366
We'll keep fighting.

